{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For I run</b> — like אָרוּץ (I run), and like it מְרוּצָתָם (their running). Some say: אָרוּץ, after the troop, in the manner of אֶרְדֹּף (I pursue), that he is found with others and sometimes alone. And the meaning is: through you alone I defeat the many." "And the meaning of <b>through you</b> — with you, or in your name that I call."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:39.914475471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}